WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:05.291
No machine simply balances itself because its design looks symmetrical.

2
00:00:05.391 --> 00:00:11.781
Accelerometers and gyroscopes report motion. Other sensors can estimate altitude and

3
00:00:11.831 --> 00:00:17.581
position. Control software compares measurements with the intended trajectory and

4
00:00:17.631 --> 00:00:21.025
commands actuators. Then it measures again.

5
00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:27.221
This loop repeats continuously. The challenge is not only making corrections quickly.

6
00:00:27.506 --> 00:00:34.606
It is making sure the system remains safe when a sensor, motor, or power supply fails.

7
00:00:34.881 --> 00:00:40.105
An inertial measurement unit can report angular rates and specific acceleration.

8
00:00:40.516 --> 00:00:45.416
Other sensors may estimate height, position and relative motion.

9
00:00:45.676 --> 00:00:49.176
But every measurement contains noise and bias.

10
00:00:49.251 --> 00:00:54.501
A flight controller must combine observations to estimate the state of the vehicle

11
00:00:54.626 --> 00:00:57.549
rather than react blindly to one number.

12
00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:02.871
Once the system estimates its state, a controller compares that estimate against the

13
00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:09.321
desired orientation, speed or path. It computes actuator commands that reduce the

14
00:01:09.421 --> 00:01:15.956
error. Control loops must account for response delay, available thrust, actuator

15
00:01:16.006 --> 00:01:18.250
limits and coupling between axes.

16
00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:23.545
Aggressive correction without stability analysis can create oscillation.

17
00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.470
Engineering confidence requires more than a perfect test run.

18
00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:35.020
Sensor failures, stuck actuators, power loss, gusts and uncertain landing conditions

19
00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:40.158
must be considered. The aircraft also needs defined safe responses.

20
00:01:40.682 --> 00:01:46.832
The details of Tesla’s unpublished control computer remain unknown; our model

21
00:01:46.932 --> 00:01:49.896
illustrates general flight-control principles.
